WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:06.939
Miroslav - thanks for receiving us here at
the Yale Divinity School at Yale University,

00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:07.990
New Haven.

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:11.910
You are professor here for Faith and Culture.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:21.720
To introduce you to the audience of the Nexus
Institute: where do you come from, and why

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.840
have you chosen to become a theologian?

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:35.660
I was born in what was then Yugoslavia, and
I was born to a man who was a minister.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:42.929
Most of our life revolved around faith and
the life of a small community, and I promptly

00:00:42.929 --> 00:00:46.180
rebelled when I was about 13 years of age.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:56.629
Then I discovered faith when I was 16, and
from then on I couldn't quite help myself

00:00:56.629 --> 00:01:03.690
but think through the basic issues of faith,
which are the basic issues of human existence.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:09.979
And, by the way, at that time in Yugoslavia,
being a theologian was really cool.

00:01:09.979 --> 00:01:17.531
It was something that had to do not just with
my existence, but also with opposition to

00:01:17.531 --> 00:01:21.450
the reigning regime.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:28.399
We thought we were doing something counter-cultural,
something on which the future, not only of

00:01:28.399 --> 00:01:35.439
our lives, but of our country and the world
depended.

00:01:35.439 --> 00:01:47.939
We live in a time in which a vast majority
of people will realize that, to save the world,

00:01:47.939 --> 00:01:55.229
we have science and technology, and politics
can play a role, international law will play

00:01:55.229 --> 00:01:56.229
a role.

00:01:56.229 --> 00:02:01.060
But what is it that theology has to offer
to the world?

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:10.340
Well, theology is about, in many ways, reflection
on the nature of human existence, the problem

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:13.370
of human existence.

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:22.300
And theology can attend to global issues of
justice, but what theology also does is that

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:30.220
it zeroes in on the deep recesses of the human
heart and human desire.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:38.540
It tries to examine who we as human beings
are as connected to what is it that we identify

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:45.270
with, project ourselves into; how the dynamics
of our desire functions.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:56.520
I think that we can't save the world unless
we save the desire of each human being.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:00.420
Theology has very much to say about this.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:09.470
But what's the difference between philosophy,
psychology, social sciences and theology?

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:19.720
Theology, at least Christian theology, thematizes
the world and human beings, not just in themselves.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:27.070
It thematizes them as themselves only as they
are related to something that's beyond the

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:31.250
boundary of this world, that's beyond the
boundary of their existence.

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:39.510
In other words, it thematizes human beings
as fundamentally related to transcendence, so that

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:45.060
the world is not just cosmos, the world is
creation.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:51.760
The world is a gift, and therefore always
more than what appears to our senses.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:04:00.060
In the world it is always the case that more
than the world is the case, to quote Sloterdijk's

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:04.320
comment about secularism.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:07.620
This is what theology brings to our attention.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:14.840
In our own lives, we are always more than
just ourselves, we live excentric existences.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:20.640
And this reference of the entire world and
human beings to transcendence is fundamental

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:21.640
to us.

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:28.750
I think that if we do not think of human beings
in those terms, we cannot understand who human

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:34.251
beings are, we cannot understand what the
problem of human existence is, and we certainly

00:04:34.251 --> 00:04:40.120
cannot imagine what salvation might look like.

